  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the young man as the subject of the Holocaust joke",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the young man, who is the central figure in the meme. The meme's structure, with the top text describing a mundane scenario and the bottom text 'holocaust', forces the viewer to associate the young man with the Holocaust. This creates a semiotic projection where the user, as the viewer, is implicitly positioned as the one who is 'finally gets naked with girl in shower' and is being equated with the Holocaust. The projection is not explicit with deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you', but the visual-textual juxtaposition creates an implicit identification where the user is the subject of the absurd and offensive comparison. The young man's cheerful expression and the mundane context further emphasize the shock value, making the user feel implicated in the joke's premise.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
